course: dictionary
lesson: 15443
title: Steamroller: a machine and a word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A steamroller is a heavy machine with big, wide rollers. It flattens new roads so the surface is smooth and firm. The clue is in the name: the machine is heavy, so it presses the road flat. «The steamroller flattened the new road before the cars could drive on it.»
explain: Today most road rollers run on diesel, not steam, but people still call them steamrollers. Steamroller can also be a verb, and then it is informal. «Our team steamrollered the other team and won 6-0.» Nobody was flattened by a machine here. It means the team beat them easily, with great power.
explain: Use the words around the word to decide its meaning. If a machine, a road or a roller is in the sentence, it is the machine. If a team, a leader or a plan is in the sentence, it is the verb, meaning to force something through or to defeat someone easily. «The head teacher steamrollered the new rule through without asking the class.» She pushed it through and ignored their objections.
fact: A steamroller is a heavy machine with big, wide rollers that flattens roads.
fact: Steamrollers were once powered by steam; now most are powered by diesel and are often called road rollers.
fact: As a verb, «steamroller» is informal and means to force something through or defeat someone easily, ignoring objections.
fact: «Steamrollered» means beaten easily, or pushed through without listening to anyone.
fact: A steamroller can also be a force that crushes all opposition, as in «The new champion was a steamroller on the court.»
exercise: «The steamroller flattened the new road.» What does steamroller mean here? | *A heavy machine that flattens roads | A kind of cooking pan | A small boat that runs on steam | A fast train with no driver
exercise: «Our team steamrollered the other team and won 6-0.» What does steamrollered mean? | Cooked them in steam | Helped them up off the grass | *Beat them easily, with great power | Lost badly after a long game
exercise: Nadia says a steamroller can only ever be a big machine. Why is she wrong? | *It can also be a verb meaning to force something through | It means soft and gentle | It is a kind of bird | It can only be a noun for a train
test: «The captain steamrollered his plan through without asking anyone.» What does steamrollered mean here? | Asked everyone for their ideas | Folded it up neatly | *Forced it through, ignoring objections | Lost the plan in the rain
test: What usually powers a steamroller today? | Steam | Wind | Water | *Diesel
exam: Which sentence uses steamroller as a verb? | «The steamroller stopped at the traffic lights.» | *«The coach steamrollered the other side with a huge win.» | «The steamroller was yellow and very noisy.» | «The steamroller rolled slowly down the road.»
